      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ashland City was incorporated in 1859, adding “City” to its original name after the town was founded in 1856.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashland_City%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The courthouse square began as a 50‑acre parcel bought from James Lenox, with a temporary courthouse erected shortly thereafter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashland_City%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The temporary courthouse was replaced by the present courthouse in 1869, solidifying the town’s civic center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashland_City%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ashland City sits on the northeast bank of the Cumberland River, a few miles upstream from its confluence with the Harpeth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashland_City%2C_Tennessee",
